(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// The abstract protocol (CPython's Objects/abstract.c and object.c): what the machine and the"] [6 1 "// built-ins call, dispatching on the types' slots with CPython's fallbacks. PY5c owns the data"] [7 1 "// model's rules (descriptors, the reflected operand of a subclass first, __getattr__)."] [11 1 "// Repr is repr(o)."] [17 19 "// a str subclass's instance too, its str value (PyObject_Repr, PyObject_Str; PY6c)"] [21 1 "// ReprObject is PyObject_Repr: __repr__'s result as it is, a str subclass's instance kept."] [42 1 "// StrOf is str(o)."] [52 1 "// StrObject is PyObject_Str: __str__'s result as it is, a str subclass's instance kept."] [73 1 "// Hash is hash(o)."] [87 1 "// identityHash is object.__hash__: a stable number per object (id(o) >> 4 in CPython; here a"] [88 1 "// counter, survey §6.4's identity)."] [100 2 "// a tracked object keeps its number in its record, so hashing does not keep it alive (finalize.go, queue 218)"] [114 2 "// a container is tracked for its number (queue 418), as a weak reference tracks an instance: in identities it, and"] [115 2 "// everything it holds, stayed alive for the program's life. pickle's memo, copy.deepcopy's, json's markers and"] [116 2 "// reprlib take id() of every container they meet, so a list pickled once kept its items past gc.collect()"] [117 2 "// (_test_multiprocessing's test_release_task_refs: the task arguments sent by a manager's or a process pool's"] [118 2 "// pickling). The record has no work, so the object's death only drops it (goFinalized)."] [136 1 "// identityTracked is whether identityHash keeps o's number in a record of its own (queue 418): a tuple, set, list or"] [137 1 "// dictionary, the containers id() is taken of to remember them, that can take a Go finalizer (finTrackable; a list's"] [138 1 "// or a dictionary's may be tracemalloc's once it traced, tmCleanup's, as cyIsNode's rule). The rest (types,"] [139 1 "// functions, modules: long-lived, and hashed as dictionaries' keys) stay in identities."] [153 1 "// lastIdentity is the last number identityHash gave (instances keep theirs in their ident, tracked objects in their"] [154 1 "// record, the rest in identities: queue 218)."] [157 1 "// Truthy is bool(o)."] [178 1 "// BinaryOp is a op b (binary_op1): a's method, then b's reflected one, b's first when b's type is a"] [179 1 "// proper subtype of a's that overrides it; NotImplemented from both a TypeError."] [192 3 "// PyNumber_Multiply's sequence_repeat"] [203 1 "// numberFast is binary_op1 of two exact ints, or of exact floats and ints (202b: the common operations without"] [204 1 "// the slots' lookups and conversions): int's method, else float's, as binary_op1 would find them; ok false when"] [205 1 "// the operands are of other types or the method answers NotImplemented."] [250 1 "// floatFast is floatBinary's +, -, * and / (by a divisor not zero) of two doubles (an int operand converted as"] [251 1 "// intToFloat converts one that fits in int64); ok false for the others (queue 210: spectral_norm's mixed operands)."] [268 1 "// tpName is a type's tp_name: a built-in type of another module than builtins named with it."] [276 1 "// seqConcatError is PyNumber_Add's sequence fallback when neither operand adds: str's, list's and tuple's sq_concat"] [277 1 "// and the bytes-like buffers' refuse b in their own words (nil for any other a)."] [296 1 "// overridesReflected is b's type a proper subtype of a's whose reflected method is its own."] [306 1 "// binRDunders are the reflected methods' names, __radd__ ..., made once (queue 305: binaryOp1 made one per call)."] [340 1 "// InPlaceOp is a op= b: the in-place method, else BinaryOp."] [343 17 "// int and float have no in-place methods"] [366 1 "// UnaryOp is +o, -o or ~o."] [377 1 "// RichCompare is a op b (PyObject_RichCompare: the C level's recursion check, then do_richcompare)."] [379 2 "// two exact ints or two exact floats: their own comparison, which recurses into nothing (202b)"] [399 1 "// doRichCompare is do_richcompare: b's swapped method first when b's type is a proper subtype of a's (whether or not"] [400 1 "// it overrides it), then a's method, then b's swapped one unless already tried (checked_reverse_op), then identity for"] [401 1 "// == and != (queue 264: test_binop's test_comparison_orders)."] [433 1 "// Eq is a == b as a Go bool (identity first, as PyObject_RichCompareBool)."] [445 1 "// GetAttr is getattr(o, name)."] [460 1 "// Call is f(*args) with the last len(kwnames) of args keyword arguments."] [469 1 "// GetIter is iter(o)."] [480 1 "// mappingOnly is an object whose subscription is mp_subscript alone, no sq_item for PySequence_Check: a union, a class"] [481 1 "// whose metaclass defines no __getitem__ (type's GetItem slot is the class subscription; queue 225: iter(int))."] [493 1 "// Next is next(it): (nil, nil) at the end."] [502 1 "// GetItem is o[key]."] [504 2 "// an exact list's or tuple's item at an int in range: the slot's answer without its conversions (202b)"] [535 1 "// seqIter is the iterator of a type with __getitem__ and no __iter__ (PY5b: its type registered)."] [574 1 "// isSeqRepeat is a type with sq_repeat."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[36 22] [67 22] [90 27] [97 27] [181 39] [188 36] [216 49] [227 39] [233 49] [342 39] [345 36] [355 36] [368 34] [382 23] [386 25] [405 30] [412 36] [418 36] [449 32] [471 29] [505 24] [513 28] [523 32] [526 23] [527 41] [561 29]]} (go/file "abstract.go" :imports [

